{"title":"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The national debt of the United States is on track to reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/8/a48e1d91fe9825fd8da1716895ffb5de56001ac3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\times10^{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> dollars by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/b/7fbc2e362b78c30c74e3604cb5d95dd655e95ae6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2033$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" />. How many digits does this number of dollars have when written as a numeral in base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />? (The approximation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/4/4342fe6348ed80ac986ce8265a5af6d3d60f27f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{10} 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"17\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/5/a3588bb395f693f5fd014687a9b680837fd2dc6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> is sufficient for this problem)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d87bb47d5646c56283191e7d49bb9a7ab977205.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 18 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 20 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 22 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 24 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"401\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Generally, the number of digits of number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> in base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/f/8cff7b974f9400c771c076fcccbf7bdd0479379b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lfloor \\log_b n \\rfloor + 1.\\]\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" />\nIn this question, it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/f/b0fe2fa2b5af4eda728abd3dcc4feb22c9cbcf72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor \\log_{5} (5\\times 10^{13})\\rfloor+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"158\" height=\"21\" />.\nNote that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/6/3d6fb7329308cd247d03a1e913faa9ba958db5cb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\log_{5} (5\\times 10^{13}) &amp;= 1+\\frac{13}{\\log_{10} 5} \\\\ &amp;\\approx 1+\\frac{13}{0.7} \\\\ &amp;\\approx 19.5 \\end{align*}\" width=\"215\" height=\"105\" />\nHence, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/2/672657f688c13d3177512cd00ebb1aabe27d9c83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{\\textbf{(B)} 20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"64\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~tsun26 (small modification by notknowanything)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/3/8b35c42f640c9269caf9cac6dc5472aed1be7485.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\times 10^{13} = 2^{13} \\cdot 5^{14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"149\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/4/0f4ce6a9c3ecabb7f81f0e5f6fc86ed40ffbc04d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{13} = 8192$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" />. Converting this to base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/5/9650db2c547986220a6e6097c822c0c77262de43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$230232$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> (trust me it doesn't take that long). So the final number in base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/5/9650db2c547986220a6e6097c822c0c77262de43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$230232$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> zeroes at the end, which gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/9/6b94a48975351f8d3ad5339b97325d82b9d448c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 + 14 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> digits. So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/2/672657f688c13d3177512cd00ebb1aabe27d9c83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{\\textbf{(B)} 20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"64\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~sidkris\n</p><p>Note - Base Conversion Step \n</p><p>To convert the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/2/dd20ed3f7741e7629c82debb6817ceb4833d75a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8192$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> from base 10 to base 5, we follow these steps:\n</p><p>1. Divide the number by 5 repeatedly, noting the quotient and remainder each time.\n</p><p>2. Stop when the quotient becomes 0, then read the remainders from bottom to top.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/4/284e257858bf3481315d21755ef23b96cace4c83.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[8192 \\div 5 = 1638 \\text{ remainder } 2\\]\" width=\"220\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7afa9b439fd2ad29485b054f38077b1785f2eddf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1638 \\div 5 = 327 \\text{ remainder } 3\\]\" width=\"210\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/c/03c33511983e11922672c750b2f31786785323a4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[327 \\div 5 = 65 \\text{ remainder } 2\\]\" width=\"193\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/2/3a2a4948d78a06071514fdb9c207f5e2b5de758e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[65 \\div 5 = 13 \\text{ remainder } 0\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/a/4ea2d691bc0f3c0ed5ed979d267fb767d7476df2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[13 \\div 5 = 2 \\text{ remainder } 3\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/2/012bc0c597d085722496bd9cd488e45101b40262.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 \\div 5 = 0 \\text{ remainder } 2\\]\" width=\"166\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Now, reading the remainders from bottom to top:<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/2/952289a08dd5d5e7b6f3f7ebfc5cc9c30adbcb3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 3, 0, 2, 3, 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/2/dd20ed3f7741e7629c82debb6817ceb4833d75a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8192$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> in base 5 is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/0/4803803846aa0d6dafaac6380cc31dff49f00322.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{230232_5}\\]\" width=\"73\" height=\"26\" />\n~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Cyantist\">luckuso</a>\n</p><p>Note - an approximation you can use here to convert 8192 to base 5: since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/3/7c368490079fe7e1b3c350e6436de634b432d12f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^5 = 3125$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/c/8fcd93bbd02b92890fadffab5164b9a4fca2897f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^6 = 15625$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" />, we automatically know that you need 6 digits to represent <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e32fb2597fb8173821caad171b7704d8c5e003.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{13}$\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> in base 5. \n</p><p>~ RushilYeole\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/3/7532bd30d03092a07ac7c927ce0ab2670bc4ed2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 10^{13} = 5 \\times (5^{13} \\times 2^{13}) = 2^{13} \\times 5^{14} = 8192 \\times 5^{14}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"407\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/3/7c368490079fe7e1b3c350e6436de634b432d12f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^5 = 3125$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/c/8fcd93bbd02b92890fadffab5164b9a4fca2897f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^6 = 15625$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" /> (or just notice that it must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/1/b21226a328df578d87c9ccf7b578c09057996330.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&gt; 8192$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" />) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/5/ec5c932beaef307daecae0fab88f76c638a9e439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies 5^5 &lt; 8192 &lt; 5^6 \\implies 5^{19} &lt; 5 \\times 10^{13} &lt; 5^{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"372\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Since an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> digits when it satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/2/752c059598cc59d83cb547ab342a62a9e1f9741c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{n-1} \\le x &lt; a^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"115\" height=\"19\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/b/39b5b2c96ff3b4e04c9b31192778a54a38815fa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 10^{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> requires <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/2/672657f688c13d3177512cd00ebb1aabe27d9c83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{\\textbf{(B)} 20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"64\" height=\"30\" /> base-5 digits.\n</p><p>~drnez\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FUsMSwb-JUc\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FUsMSwb-JUc</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution 2 by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/AKLPjTRPF4Q\">https://youtu.be/AKLPjTRPF4Q</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B\">2024 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/